# T-1026: Two sibling dicts each containing an identity function have independent TypeVars.
# dict1.f and dict2.f have separate fresh TypeVar instantiations — unifying one does
# not constrain the other. This is a basic acceptance test verifying that two [fn [let x] x]
# bindings in sibling dicts are not accidentally merged into the same TypeVar.
# Absence of === warn asserts both definitions type-check cleanly with zero warnings.
[
  dict1: [f: [fn [let x] x]]
  dict2: [f: [fn [let y] y]]
  result: True
]
=== out
Dict({"dict1": Dict({"f": Function(x)}), "dict2": Dict({"f": Function(y)}), "result": Bool(true)})
